1
00:00:01,070 --> 00:00:02,930
So you live in this neighborhood.

2
00:00:03,810 --> 00:00:05,430
I was just here not long ago.

3
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:09,210
We're almost there. I'll head off now.

4
00:00:10,860 --> 00:00:12,620
Also,

5
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:14,990
you don't have to do this next time.

6
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:27,970
Does what happened today

7
00:00:28,140 --> 00:00:30,270
count as spending the night together?

8
00:00:31,390 --> 00:00:34,720
-Can you stop bringing up spending the night—
-You're back.

9
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:42,450
I've been waiting for you
at home for a while now.

10
00:00:42,450 --> 00:00:43,550
Have you had

11
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:44,990
dinner yet?

12
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:50,290
Hello,

13
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:53,180
I'm Yoo Taeseok,
a close friend of Yihyun.

14
00:00:56,920 --> 00:00:58,120
Hello.

15
00:00:58,280 --> 00:01:01,400
I'm the one starring
in Director Jung Yihyun's musical,

16
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:03,670
Kang Jae-on.

17
00:01:11,930 --> 00:01:13,500
Tell me honestly,

18
00:01:13,670 --> 00:01:15,110
what's your relationship with that guy?

19
00:01:15,110 --> 00:01:16,900
There's nothing between us.

20
00:01:26,530 --> 00:01:28,390
Hyung.

21
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:33,590
What are you thinking about?

22
00:01:33,770 --> 00:01:36,130
What's got you so focused?
You didn't even hear me call you.

23
00:01:36,130 --> 00:01:37,580
Ah...

24
00:01:38,229 --> 00:01:39,380
Well...

25
00:01:40,190 --> 00:01:41,690
Just random thoughts.

26
00:01:44,430 --> 00:01:47,100
I'm Yoo Taeseok, a close friend of Yihyun.

27
00:01:47,270 --> 00:01:47,820
Hah.

28
00:01:47,990 --> 00:01:49,390
A close friend of Yihyun.

29
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:50,100
Who asked?

30
00:01:50,270 --> 00:01:51,009
Tsk.

31
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:52,280
Hey.

32
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:54,960
In your eyes,

33
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:56,640
how am I?

34
00:01:57,820 --> 00:01:58,940
You?

35
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:00,630
Well...

36
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:01,840
Pretty energetic.

37
00:02:01,930 --> 00:02:02,840
Very energetic,

38
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:04,270
pretty much so.

39
00:02:04,580 --> 00:02:06,810
No, I'm not asking about
things like that.

40
00:02:06,810 --> 00:02:08,210
I'm talking about looks.

41
00:02:08,479 --> 00:02:09,850
My looks.

42
00:02:10,250 --> 00:02:13,150
You... are not my type.

43
00:02:13,310 --> 00:02:14,890
You're not mine either.

44
00:02:15,370 --> 00:02:17,960
What I'm trying to say is

45
00:02:18,130 --> 00:02:19,870
am I that average?

46
00:02:20,180 --> 00:02:21,960
Anyone can tell
there's a stark difference.

47
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:23,130
With who?

48
00:02:23,579 --> 00:02:24,630
Huh?

49
00:02:24,780 --> 00:02:26,810
Uh... It's nothing.

50
00:02:27,970 --> 00:02:29,360
I'm getting off work.

51
00:02:29,630 --> 00:02:31,800
-See you tomorrow.
-Okay.

52
00:02:35,010 --> 00:02:37,780
[Hongseok]

53
00:02:38,010 --> 00:02:40,250
[Park Seonghyun]

54
00:02:43,010 --> 00:02:45,090
[Shin Yongseok] [Shin Junseop] [Ha Yosep]

55
00:02:53,090 --> 00:02:55,540
[Play Me]

56
00:03:30,790 --> 00:03:32,530
Why is he here?

57
00:03:33,730 --> 00:03:37,260
Could it be that he stayed up all night
working part-time again?

58
00:04:12,010 --> 00:04:14,000
Is it today?

59
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:17,519
The day we spend the night together.

60
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:20,750
Answer me.

61
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:24,020
Right now.

62
00:04:25,690 --> 00:04:26,940
Right here.

63
00:04:27,420 --> 00:04:29,330
Do you want to

64
00:04:29,490 --> 00:04:31,390
spend the night together?

65
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:56,770
Oh, you're here.

66
00:04:56,770 --> 00:04:57,690
You're here.

67
00:04:57,850 --> 00:04:58,870
Hello.

68
00:04:59,010 --> 00:05:00,640
Ah, you must be the one.

69
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:01,940
What's going on? Huh?

70
00:05:01,940 --> 00:05:03,120
Did you decide to work together?

71
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:03,790
Really?

72
00:05:03,790 --> 00:05:04,600
Don't make a fuss.

73
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:05,490
Hey,

74
00:05:05,490 --> 00:05:06,600
what do you mean make a fuss?

75
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:08,520
Didn't you watch his performance
and completely fall in love...

76
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:09,320
What's wrong?

77
00:05:09,390 --> 00:05:11,640
What's wrong? Are you shy?
Is it a secret?

78
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:12,580
What's wrong?

79
00:05:14,020 --> 00:05:16,390
Then I'll leave too. Please go on.

80
00:05:16,660 --> 00:05:17,730
Wait for me!

81
00:05:18,380 --> 00:05:19,910
Ah...

82
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:21,330
so cute.

83
00:05:21,490 --> 00:05:23,090
So cute, Jung Yihyun.

84
00:05:30,110 --> 00:05:32,020
How can you let the actor do these things?

85
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:33,380
It's nothing.

86
00:05:33,570 --> 00:05:35,050
I'm very good at this.

87
00:05:35,260 --> 00:05:36,230
Leave it to me.

88
00:05:36,530 --> 00:05:38,240
I'm touched.

89
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:40,200
You're so easy to get along with.

90
00:05:41,450 --> 00:05:44,060
Completely opposite to someone.

91
00:05:44,280 --> 00:05:45,260
Speaking of,

92
00:05:45,409 --> 00:05:46,890
your personalities are worlds apart.

93
00:05:46,890 --> 00:05:48,420
How did you become friends?

94
00:05:50,970 --> 00:05:54,010
Did he say... we're friends?

95
00:05:54,170 --> 00:05:55,110
Yes.

96
00:05:55,260 --> 00:05:57,409
He said you two
were really close back in school.

97
00:05:57,409 --> 00:05:59,350
Is that not so?

98
00:06:07,390 --> 00:06:08,270
I need to take a call.

99
00:06:08,270 --> 00:06:09,150
Ah, okay.

100
00:06:09,820 --> 00:06:11,730
Hello?

101
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:41,920
I heard you told your manager

102
00:06:42,090 --> 00:06:44,130
that we are friends.

103
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:48,540
You're telling others we are friends,

104
00:06:48,690 --> 00:06:51,330
but why are you still
speaking to me so formally?

105
00:06:51,330 --> 00:06:53,680
After all, we didn't meet as friends.

106
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:26,440
Let's talk.

107
00:07:31,440 --> 00:07:33,060
Ha...

108
00:07:33,220 --> 00:07:34,220
You are really...

109
00:07:34,270 --> 00:07:35,850
hard to figure out.

110
00:07:36,930 --> 00:07:39,260
Five years ago,
you suddenly turned cold towards me.

111
00:07:39,260 --> 00:07:41,390
When I initiated a conversation,
you ignored me.

112
00:07:41,390 --> 00:07:43,390
You treated me like I was invisible.

113
00:07:43,610 --> 00:07:45,720
There must be a reason, right?

114
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:50,640
I thought we were close.

115
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:54,040
Close?

116
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:00,830
Weren't you just fooling around with me?

117
00:08:00,830 --> 00:08:02,160
Jung Yihyun.

118
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:04,810
Since he's a celebrity,

119
00:08:04,970 --> 00:08:06,860
I hung out with him a few times,

120
00:08:07,020 --> 00:08:10,360
but he's actually pretty boring.

121
00:08:16,750 --> 00:08:17,490
Jae-on,

122
00:08:17,650 --> 00:08:19,630
please come give me a hand.

123
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:26,900
Ah, okay.

124
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:33,360
Now is not the time to argue about this.

125
00:08:34,039 --> 00:08:37,020
Let's rehearse separately for a while.

126
00:08:35,030 --> 00:08:37,080
[Let's rehearse separately for a while.]

127
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:43,150
[Then when will we see each other again?]

128
00:08:40,260 --> 00:08:42,650
Then when will we see each other again?

129
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:45,510
Someday...

130
00:08:44,179 --> 00:08:45,800
[Someday...]

131
00:08:45,660 --> 00:08:47,450
Goodbye!

132
00:08:53,350 --> 00:08:54,700
Director.

133
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:56,660
Director?

134
00:08:56,060 --> 00:08:57,060
[Director?]

135
00:08:56,820 --> 00:08:57,740
Di-

136
00:08:57,060 --> 00:08:58,110
[Di?]

137
00:08:57,740 --> 00:08:58,460
rec-

138
00:08:58,110 --> 00:08:58,860
[rec?]

139
00:08:58,460 --> 00:08:59,390
tor.

140
00:08:58,860 --> 00:08:59,980
[tor?]

141
00:09:04,620 --> 00:09:06,300
Would you like to order?

142
00:09:09,630 --> 00:09:10,840
Sir?

143
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:17,240
S-Sir,

144
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:19,700
you can't take that!

145
00:09:48,510 --> 00:09:50,760
Why do I run into him everywhere?

146
00:09:53,930 --> 00:09:55,470
Hello,

147
00:09:55,630 --> 00:09:57,230
I'm at your door.

148
00:09:57,780 --> 00:09:59,640
I'll be right out with the kimchi.

149
00:09:59,770 --> 00:10:00,500
Kimchi.

150
00:10:00,660 --> 00:10:01,900
What's going on?

151
00:10:03,230 --> 00:10:04,840
Why are you here?

152
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:17,830
So,

153
00:10:18,210 --> 00:10:20,510
the pet sitter
who helped clean up last time

154
00:10:20,510 --> 00:10:23,240
and cooked for me

155
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:24,930
was you, right?

156
00:10:25,070 --> 00:10:26,210
Yes,

157
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:28,280
it was me.

158
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:31,420
Gently.

159
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:10,690
Oh.

160
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:12,200
I-It's pretty good.

161
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:13,590
N-Not good at all.

162
00:11:14,160 --> 00:11:17,120
Thank... Thank god you said it's not good.

163
00:11:21,980 --> 00:11:23,470
Why have you been

164
00:11:23,630 --> 00:11:24,920
avoiding me?

165
00:11:25,090 --> 00:11:26,820
-I didn't—
-You won't admit it.

166
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:29,050
But you ran away when you saw me

167
00:11:29,220 --> 00:11:32,220
in the cafe, the convenience store,
and on the street.

168
00:11:37,450 --> 00:11:39,190
I think there's a reason

169
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:41,760
for what you said that day

170
00:11:42,510 --> 00:11:44,930
and why you've been avoiding me.

171
00:11:45,100 --> 00:11:46,130
Close?

172
00:11:50,740 --> 00:11:53,000
Weren't you just fooling around with me?

173
00:11:53,950 --> 00:11:55,950
Tell me when you want to.

174
00:11:57,760 --> 00:12:00,220
I'm always ready to listen.

175
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:16,080
Eden,

176
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:18,700
do you really remember nothing?

177
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:21,650
Remember nothing...

178
00:12:29,090 --> 00:12:30,630
Director!

179
00:12:30,790 --> 00:12:31,350
Yes?

180
00:12:31,510 --> 00:12:34,530
Help me run the lines.

181
00:12:34,680 --> 00:12:36,200
It's really hard to get the emotions right

182
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:37,640
practicing lines alone.

183
00:12:39,590 --> 00:12:41,020
Which part?

184
00:12:41,250 --> 00:12:43,320
Act 2, Scene 4.

185
00:12:55,330 --> 00:12:56,560
Eden,

186
00:12:56,700 --> 00:12:58,670
do you really remember nothing?

187
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:00,710
We seem to be meeting for the first time.

188
00:13:00,710 --> 00:13:02,310
Have we met before?

189
00:13:05,370 --> 00:13:07,800
We agreed

190
00:13:07,970 --> 00:13:10,690
to go see the sea together
when we reunite.

191
00:13:25,250 --> 00:13:27,500
Power outage this suddenly?

192
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:30,200
I'll go check and be right back.

193
00:13:34,460 --> 00:13:36,270
Don't go.

194
00:13:41,130 --> 00:13:43,210
Don't leave me alone.

195
00:13:48,860 --> 00:13:50,870
Sit down!

196
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:54,010
I won't open the door for you
until you memorize it all.

197
00:13:54,010 --> 00:13:54,920
Got it?

198
00:14:22,710 --> 00:14:25,000
I envy Luka.

199
00:14:27,170 --> 00:14:29,660
He gets to see a sea like this every day.

200
00:14:32,390 --> 00:14:34,780
He gave up this precious sea

201
00:14:35,830 --> 00:14:38,560
to see Eden.

202
00:14:38,770 --> 00:14:40,700
So stupid.

203
00:14:40,860 --> 00:14:42,160
Is it stupid to do so?

204
00:14:42,330 --> 00:14:45,320
Eden doesn't remember him at all.

205
00:14:45,480 --> 00:14:48,290
But for a single promise,

206
00:14:48,460 --> 00:14:51,220
he gave up everything to come.

207
00:14:51,470 --> 00:14:52,770
In that case,

208
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:54,670
I'm stupid too.

209
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:57,590
What do you mean?

210
00:14:58,210 --> 00:15:03,140
We agreed to stand on stage together.

211
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:06,440
Because of our promise,

212
00:15:06,620 --> 00:15:09,340
I've persevered until now.

213
00:15:09,530 --> 00:15:12,520
I've had countless moments
wanting to give up.

214
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:15,950
Hey, it's pretty dangerous.

215
00:15:16,110 --> 00:15:18,170
Let's go down.

216
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:19,210
Come up and see.

217
00:15:19,380 --> 00:15:22,180
Standing here
feels like entering another world.

218
00:15:24,290 --> 00:15:26,040
The hand you held mine with

219
00:15:26,220 --> 00:15:27,940
was so warm

220
00:15:28,090 --> 00:15:30,380
that I can never forget it.

221
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:33,380
It helped me stand up again.

222
00:15:36,910 --> 00:15:39,850
You don't remember, do you?

223
00:15:41,660 --> 00:15:43,670
I remember.

224
00:15:49,640 --> 00:15:51,920
I've been waiting for you.

225
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:10,940
[Epilogue]

226
00:16:10,700 --> 00:16:12,760
Ah, so tired.

227
00:16:13,310 --> 00:16:16,140
What's going on?
Why is he sleeping here again?

228
00:16:16,490 --> 00:16:18,710
Instead of going home.

229
00:16:23,860 --> 00:16:26,090
I was going to sleep comfortably alone.

230
00:16:31,880 --> 00:16:33,480
Oh, so sleepy.
